                <pb facs="0737" n="731" sameAs="frus:frus1942v02/pg731"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.48/1172: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the United
                        Kingdom (Winant)</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-01-05T19:00:00-05:00">January 5, 1942—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>44. Please expedite reply to Department’s no. 5630, December 3, 11 p.m. Specific
                    information would be helpful regarding the alleged payment by the Greek
                    Government for Australian wheat shipped as far as Egypt and held there by the
                    British Government. Rumors regarding such wheat continue to circulate in Greece,
                    and Axis propaganda has not failed to take advantage of them.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
